---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Omnipeak"
  description="Omnipeak is the engineering practice of David — a software engineer in the Los Angeles / Orange County area building booking, membership, and billing systems for small businesses."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>The person building your system</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Omnipeak is the engineering practice of David — a software engineer based in the Los
        Angeles / Orange County area, currently completing a master's in computer science at
        Georgia Tech.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--rule">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Why the direct model works</h2>
        <p>
          When you hire Omnipeak, the person you talk to is the person writing the code. That
          isn't a limitation — it's the point. Nothing gets handed to a junior developer, no
          requirement gets lost between an account manager and an engineering team, and
          decisions that would take an agency a week of internal meetings happen in one
          conversation with you.
        </p>
        <p>
          The whole stack is owned end to end — from designing the database your business
          records live in, through the software itself, to deployment and keeping it running.
          One person accountable for all of it means there's never a layer to hide behind when
          something needs fixing.
        </p>

        <h2>Deliberately boring technology</h2>
        <p>
          Omnipeak builds on proven, widely used technology — TypeScript, PostgreSQL, and
          Stripe — chosen precisely because tens of thousands of developers know it. That's
          your protection: if you ever want someone else to maintain your system, you'll be
          able to find them. Clever, obscure technology is a form of lock-in; Omnipeak doesn't
          use it.
        </p>

        <h2>Why bookings and memberships</h2>
        <p>
          Reservation and billing systems look simple and aren't. Time-slot logic, recurring
          payments, failed charges, memberships that pause and resume — this is exactly where
          off-the-shelf tools run out and where half-finished custom projects tend to die.
          Specializing here means those problems have already been solved once before your
          project starts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
